# Commit after TDD slices

After migrating fixture(s) and making them pass, commit before starting the next group.

- Prefer one commit when the same implementation greens several newly unskipped goldens (`test:` rewrite/unskip together with `feat(parser):` only if the diff stays one concern; otherwise `test:` then `feat(parser):`, still before the next group).
- If one parser change knocks out multiple migrated cases in the same slice, commit once for that slice.
- Do not leave a green migrated fixture uncommitted while moving on to another construct.
- Push when the user asks, or when continuing after an explicit push request; local commit is the hard requirement per slice.
